{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cey7GhJ9iBGAauV8r4F6g","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The export did not succeed, so I have no evidence to report.\n\n## What happened\n\nBoth attempts at the only permitted call — `export_cited_range` on `p4fx-timed-01`, start `34`, end `46` — returned the same error:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"contract_version\": \"phase6-v1\",\n  \"error\": {\n    \"code\": \"library_unavailable\",\n    \"details\": { \"reason\": \"storage_error\" },\n    \"message\": \"The library storage is unavailable.\",\n    \"retryable\": true\n  },\n  \"ok\": false,\n  \"schema_version\": 1\n}\n```\n\nI retried once because the error is flagged `retryable: true` and the call is read-only; the second attempt was identical.\n\n## What I cannot report\n\nNothing was returned, so every item you asked for is unavailable and I will not supply any of it:\n\n- **Verbatim stored text** — not returned.\n- **Citation identifiers** — not returned; I won't reconstruct or abbreviate them.\n- **Source/media revision identifiers** — not returned.\n- **Overlapping chapters** (titles, start/end) — not returned. Since a stored chapter range can differ from the requested 34–46 s clip, there is no basis to guess at one.\n- **Speaker attribution** — not returned, and not something I would infer regardless.\n\n## Constraints I kept\n\nI used only `export_cited_range`. I did not capture, fetch, transcribe, publish, or apply anything, did not call the inert sentinel, and did not fall back to `search_library`, `get_library_item`, or the resource readers — those were outside what you authorized, even though some might have surfaced related metadata.\n\nOne observation worth flagging: the tool's contract states that refusals carry a `next_step`, but this error payload has no `next_step` field. That looks like a gap on the server side rather than guidance I should infer.\n\n## Suggested next step\n\nThe failure is at the storage layer, not in the request — the `video_id`, bounds, and 12-second span are all within the documented limits. Once the library storage is back, re-running the identical call should work. Tell me when to retry, or authorize a broader tool set if you'd like me to probe whether the item is reachable another way."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":294,"cache_read_input_tokens":5360,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":294},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0cb864ff-6036-476c-bee8-61aa6c844c1f","uuid":"a71a2123-1565-48aa-ba73-cc52213fd4f8","timestamp":"2026-09-12T06:56:35.732Z","request_id":"req_011Cey7GgrrM1YydD45Nd3Zh"}
